{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 c5 4. e3 Nc6 5. b3 Nf6 6. Bb2 Be7 7. Ne2 h5 8. h3 Qc7 9. O-O Bf5 10. f4 e4 { Laboratory starts here. Black establishes c5-d5-e5. White must challenge the center before completing every wing pawn move. Develop a knight to support c4 or e4, and calculate the resulting exchanges. Consider whether a partial formation gives more active play than the complete shell. } 11. dxe4 { Candidate comparison. The pawn captures a pawn on e4. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 11... dxe4 12. Nec3 Qc8 13. Kh2 h4 14. g4 Bxg4 15. hxg4 { Candidate comparison. The pawn captures a bishop on g4. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 15... Nxg4+ 16. Kh1 Nxe3 17. Qe2 Nxf1 18. Qxf1 f5 19. Bh3 { Candidate comparison. Places the bishop on h3. Compare its activity and safety with its previous square, then use the branch explanation to connect the move to a plan. } 19... Qe6 20. Nd2 Rd8 *

