{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. Nf3 Be6 5. O-O Qd7 6. b3 Bh3 7. Bxh3 Qxh3 8. e4 Nf6 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Re1 f6 { Laboratory starts here. Black exchanges the g2 bishop and brings the queen toward White's already castled king. White's knight has left g1, so the queen on h3 cannot simply be captured by that knight. Inspect checks and dark-square threats, develop with tempo if available and look for central counterplay. The king is already on g1, so the task is defending the actual shelter. } 11. d4 { Candidate comparison. Changes central space and pawn contacts. Calculate captures, advances and maintaining tension before choosing the next piece plan. } 11... O-O-O 12. c4 Nde7 13. d5 Nf5 14. Kh1 Qg4 15. Nfd2 { Candidate comparison. Places the knight on d2. Compare its activity and safety with its previous square, then use the branch explanation to connect the move to a plan. } 15... Qxd1 16. Rxd1 Ncd4 17. Nc3 h5 18. Nde4 c6 19. Rb1 { Candidate comparison. Places the rook on b1. Compare its activity and safety with its previous square, then use the branch explanation to connect the move to a plan. } 19... Bb4 20. h4 Rdg8 *

